<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds slip with Bunds as dollar remains up.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds slip with Bunds as dollar remains up.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	106.76/86 (-0.10)	   3.74 (+0.06)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   114.80/90 (-0.20)	   4.58 (+0.06)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.41/49 (-0.19)	   5.55 (+0.04)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   114.53/73 (-0.38)	   6.33 (+0.04)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	102.28 (-0.39)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (Sept)	113.72 (-0.22 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.1259 (prev 1.1258)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.026     +0.01	  10-2 yr  181	182</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.07	-0.07	  10-5 yr   98	 99</p>
<p> Long	 -0.07	-0.07</p>
<p>-------------------------(July 15)------------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds end way down as dollar strength disturbs market, but long-term sentiment intact as no German repo hike expected.</p>
<p>* Dealers say activity mainly professional, focuses on well-bought Feb 2007 benchmark and long bond.</p>
<p>* Yield gaps with Germany and curve itself broadly unchanged.</p>
